1. Definitions

"Software" means ZestEngine as provided by the Licensor: the engine
runtime, the editor, the hub, the tools, their source code, compiled
binaries, shaders, built-in assets and documentation, and any part of them.
Shader source, include files, shader libraries, and compiled or baked
shader programs (including SPIR-V and specialized variants) are covered.
Separately licensed third-party material is governed by section 6.

"Licensor" means Ryno Kotze, the copyright holder of the Software.

"You" means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this
license, including your employees and contractors acting for you.

"Product" means a game, application, interactive experience, virtual event
or other work that you create with the Software, in which the Software (or
part of it) is included only in compiled, object-code form as a component
of that work and not as a standalone engine, editor, SDK or tool.

"Modification" means any change to, addition to, or work derived from the
Software or any part of its source code, including code copied from the
Software into another project.
Translations to another language or graphics API, adaptations,
renaming, and reformatting of covered code are also Modifications; they do
not remove the conditions of this license.

"Distribution" includes making a copy available to another person or
entity, whether free of charge or for payment. Offering remote access to
the engine, editor, SDK or tools as a service is also subject to section
3(b). Operating a game or application that qualifies as a Product is
permitted under section 2.


