3. Restrictions

You may not:

  a. publish, distribute, sell, rent or otherwise make available to anyone
     else the source code of the Software or of any Modification, whether
     publicly (for example in a public repository) or privately, except as
     allowed in section 4;

  b. distribute the Software or a Modification as a standalone engine,
     editor, SDK, framework, library or tool, or as part of any product
     whose main purpose is to provide reusable engine or development-tool
     functionality to others. You may not use the Software or a
     Modification to offer a competing engine, editor, SDK, rendering
     library, shader library or development tool, including as a hosted
     service. This restriction applies to offerings using the Software;
     it does not prohibit independently developed software;

  c. remove, alter or hide any copyright, license or attribution notice in
     the Software;

  d. sublicense the Software, or grant anyone rights in it beyond those
     this license gives You;

  e. use the name "ZestEngine", the Licensor's name or any related logo to
     suggest that the Licensor endorses You or your Product, except for the
     factual attribution required by section 5, which must not imply
     endorsement;

  f. claim that You or anyone else originally authored the Software or
     its covered portions, or misrepresent a Modification as an original
     or official ZestEngine release. You may accurately identify and take
     credit for your own contributions without concealing their origin;

  g. extract or repackage covered shaders or other components for separate
     distribution, whether as source, compiled programs, asset packs or
     libraries, except for the sharing expressly allowed in section 4.
     Adapting them for another engine or changing their names does not grant
     permission for such distribution.


4. Allowed sharing of source code

You may share the source code of the Software or of your Modifications
only:

  a. with your own employees and contractors who are working on your
     Product, as long as they are bound by this license and do not share it
     further;

  b. with the Licensor, for example as a proposed contribution to the
     official ZestEngine project. By submitting a contribution You grant
     the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable license
     to use, reproduce, modify, publicly display, sublicense and distribute
     your contribution as part of the Software under any terms. You retain
     ownership of your original contribution and confirm that You have the
     rights needed to grant this license. Identify any third-party material
     and its terms when submitting it;

  c. as public excerpts containing at most 30 lines of Software source
     code per discussion, solely to explain a bug, ask for support or
     discuss the Software. Include the ZestEngine name, a link to the
     official repository, and a reference to this license. Do not split
     or combine excerpts to publish a larger portion of the Software or
     provide a reusable shader, library or other component; and

  d. as public patch files submitted to the official project for review
     and contribution, containing your changes and only the original
     source context reasonably necessary to review or apply them. This
     permission does not extend to publishing complete replacement files,
     source archives, mirrors or independently distributed engine forks.

Recipients of excerpts and patches receive no permission to use the
Software beyond this license. Preserve applicable notices and identify
changes. These exceptions do not override third-party restrictions.

Sharing an unmodified link to the official ZestEngine source location is
always allowed.
The official repository is https://github.com/lemonxah/zestengine.


5. Attribution

  a. Every Product that includes the Software, or any part of it, must give
     visible credit to ZestEngine in the Product itself, in at least one
     place a user can reasonably find, such as the credits screen, the
     "about" screen or a start-up splash screen. The credit must read
     "Made with ZestEngine" or "Powered by ZestEngine", and must include
     a link to the official ZestEngine website or source location where the
     Product's format allows a link.

     A Product using only ZestEngine shaders or rendering components may
     instead use "Includes ZestEngine rendering technology". Attribution
     remains required for modified, translated, compiled or baked versions of
     covered code. For a Product without a graphical user interface, place
     the credit in its user-facing help or documentation. A splash screen
     is not required if another permitted location provides the credit.

  b. If the Product has a store page, website or documentation that lists
     the technologies it uses, ZestEngine must be named there as well.

  c. Any copy of the Software's source code that You keep, including your
     Modifications, must keep this license file and the copyright notices
     it contains, subject to the excerpt and patch formats in section 4.

  d. Every distributed Product containing the Software must include a
     readable copy of this license and the accompanying ZestEngine NOTICE
     file in its legal notices, documentation or distribution files.
     Supplying those files does not replace the visible credit in 5(a).
     Compilation or optimization may omit source comments from executable
     code, provided the required notices accompany the Product. This is
     not permission to remove notices from source copies.

  e. Mark modified source files with a notice identifying the modifier,
     date and a brief description of the changes. If You distribute a
     Product containing Modifications, state in its legal notices that it
     uses a modified version of ZestEngine. You do not have to publish your
     source code or a detailed change log to comply with this requirement.


